Get me to a hospital.

53
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:38,280
All right, so very interesting.

54
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:46,590
All the gifts that they got and definitely very useful because this is a very common items that you get for babies, right?

55
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:48,120
That's right.

56
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:55,750
This stuff is really, really valuable because if you have a baby or if your brother or sister has a baby, you'll notice that these are very common items.

57
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:58,990
So let's go through a couple of them in today's Language Takeaway.

58
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:02,740
Language Takeaway.

59
00:03:04,210 --> 00:03:10,210
Okay, so the first word that we're going to take a look at, the most common one and useful one for a baby is a bib.

60
00:03:10,650 --> 00:03:11,050
Bib.

61
00:03:11,570 --> 00:03:13,130
So, babies are messy.

62
00:03:13,840 --> 00:03:16,480
When they eat food, they get their food on their clothes.

63
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:19,370
So to protect the clothes, babies wear bibs.

64
00:03:19,730 --> 00:03:22,310
This is a piece of cloth or fabric around their neck.

65
00:03:22,830 --> 00:03:23,910
Okay, a bib.

66
00:03:25,160 --> 00:03:33,000
And also, sometimes you want to go out with your baby to the mall, you're walking and you don't want to carry him in your arms all the time.

67
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:34,580
So you need a stroller.

68
00:03:35,150 --> 00:03:39,210
Okay, so basically a stroller is a chair on wheels for a baby.

69
00:03:39,810 --> 00:03:42,690
Babies are heavy and as they get older, they get heavier.

70
00:03:43,090 --> 00:03:46,750
And so this is a way to push the baby around, not carry the baby.

71
00:03:46,930 --> 00:03:49,990
Right, and maybe the baby falls asleep, so they can fall asleep in the stroller.

72
00:03:50,250 --> 00:03:50,510
Exactly.

73
00:03:50,890 --> 00:03:56,090
Okay, and while talking about chairs, we're going to take a look at two different types of chairs.

74
00:03:57,060 --> 00:03:58,450
First one is a high chair.

75
00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:00,180
Okay, high chair.

76
00:04:00,220 --> 00:04:03,100
Think about the word high, that means tall in this case.

77
00:04:03,580 --> 00:04:06,880
A high chair is a chair for babies at the table.

78
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:11,200
So if you put a baby on a regular chair, they can't eat with adults.

79
00:04:11,480 --> 00:04:12,360
Right, they're too small.

80
00:04:12,560 --> 00:04:18,020
So we give them high chairs so that they can sit a little bit higher and they can be at the table with adults.

81
00:04:18,340 --> 00:04:18,660
Exactly.

82
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:20,460
So they're very common.

83
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:26,790
For example, you go to a restaurant, they will have a little high chairs if you have a baby or a small child.

84
00:04:27,110 --> 00:04:30,040
So if you're at a restaurant, you have a baby, you ask for a high chair.

85
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:32,240
You say, do you have a high chair, please?

86
00:04:32,240 --> 00:04:33,420
Yeah, perfect.

87
00:04:33,420 --> 00:04:44,600
And well, if you're going to the restaurant or you go anywhere in your car, you need to have the baby be safe and obviously they can't fit on a normal seat.

88
00:04:45,390 --> 00:04:46,350
No, with a seat belt?

89
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:47,470
No, I don't think so.

90
00:04:47,670 --> 00:04:49,730
So that's why you get them a car seat.

91
00:04:50,290 --> 00:04:57,630
Okay, a car seat is a special chair that goes on the seat of the car and usually it's very, very safe.

92
00:04:58,240 --> 00:05:00,370
It's made to protect the baby.

93
00:05:00,840 --> 00:05:01,840
Right.

94
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:06,130
So if you are ever in a car accident, the car seat will help protect the small baby.

95
00:05:06,450 --> 00:05:06,570
Right.

96
00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:10,360
So it's supposed to go in the back of the car, not the front.

97
00:05:10,360 --> 00:05:10,950
Yes, always.

98
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:12,800
Very good.

99
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:15,070
And now moving on to our last two words.

100
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:21,540
If you're at home, you sometimes want to have the baby play and you get them a play pen.

101
00:05:21,540 --> 00:05:27,450
So basically this is a way for parents to leave the baby playing but not look at the baby the whole time.

102
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:28,720
Right.

103
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:34,020
A play pen is like a cage for a baby, but it's soft and it's cute and it's pretty.

104
00:05:34,020 --> 00:05:42,200
So it's basically like an open area that's protected on the sides and the baby can go inside but the baby can't leave.

105
00:05:42,200 --> 00:05:43,200
Right.

106
00:05:43,200 --> 00:05:49,310
It's like a cage basically and it has little toys and that's the way you just keep them in there for a while.

107
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:51,520
Exactly.

108
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:52,520
All right.

109
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:57,680
And now when you want to put the baby to sleep, it can't obviously sleep in a big bed because it might roll over, it might fall off.

110
00:05:57,680 --> 00:06:00,110
There's a lot of things that can go wrong, so you get them a crib.

111
00:06:00,650 --> 00:06:00,850
Right.

112
00:06:00,970 --> 00:06:02,750
So a crib is a bed for babies.

113
00:06:03,170 --> 00:06:08,630
This is usually high off the ground and it's usually quite small and the baby can't climb out of it.

114
00:06:09,200 --> 00:06:10,200
Right.

115
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:11,200
Yeah.

116
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:14,840
So it's a very safe bed so the baby can't fall out, can't climb out.

117
00:06:14,840 --> 00:06:15,840
Exactly.

118
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:16,840
Very good.

119
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:21,370
So very interesting, very useful things for you if you're having a baby, planning on getting these things.

