147
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:38,440
Okay, so at the beginning of the dialogue, the woman receives a bib for the baby and she says, this will definitely come in handy.

148
00:07:38,440 --> 00:07:40,100
To come in handy.

149
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:44,160
Right, so when something comes in handy, it means it will be useful.

150
00:07:44,700 --> 00:07:47,220
Okay, so something that's handy is useful.

151
00:07:47,940 --> 00:07:49,980
To come in handy means to be useful.

152
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:51,760
It will be useful in the future.

153
00:07:52,920 --> 00:07:59,400
So for example, you should take a flashlight with you in the car just in case because it could come in handy.

154
00:07:59,400 --> 00:07:59,610
That's right.

155
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:04,530
Or if I know that Marco is traveling to India, I can give him a map of India.

156
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:08,040
I say, Marco, this map might come in handy.

157
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:09,040
Exactly.

158
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:09,310
Very good.

159
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:14,190
So to come in handy or in something that is handy, something that's useful.

160
00:08:15,680 --> 00:08:22,080
And towards the end, a very popular phrase you probably heard in every movie that has like maybe a pregnant woman in there.

161
00:08:23,120 --> 00:08:24,360
My water just broke.

162
00:08:24,560 --> 00:08:25,180
My water broke.

163
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:28,760
Okay, so the woman says, my water broke.

164
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:29,560
Take me to the hospital.

165
00:08:29,760 --> 00:08:30,760
Right.

166
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:34,840
Okay, so this means I'm having my baby right now.

167
00:08:34,840 --> 00:08:37,300
So why do they say that the water broke?

168
00:08:37,480 --> 00:08:39,980
Because actually water kind of breaks, right?

169
00:08:40,040 --> 00:08:43,200
I think there's a protective water cushion.

170
00:08:43,200 --> 00:08:45,880
Basically there's a sack of water protecting the baby.

171
00:08:45,880 --> 00:08:46,880
It's not just water.

172
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:48,870
It's all sorts of like body fluids.

173
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:59,510
And basically when that breaks, it comes out and you know that you're going to have the baby because that means the baby has to come out now because that protective fluid is gone.

174
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:03,250
Maybe the baby just kind of kicks that water out and just like, I'm ready to come out.

175
00:09:03,450 --> 00:09:04,630
I have no idea how it works.

176
